# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Android (Capacitor) build config — API server for online sync
#
# The packaged app is fully offline-first: books, PDFs, favorites and settings
# live in the on-device IndexedDB cache and work with NO server at all.
# When a network is available, the app syncs with your Dar-ul-Uloom API server.
# There is NO runtime URL prompt — the server address is baked in here at
# build time, so this file must exist before you run `npm run build:android`.
#
# To point the app at your deployed server:
#   1. Deploy the API (see README — Render blueprint or any Node host).
#   2. Set VITE_API_BASE below to that server's origin, e.g.:
#        VITE_API_BASE=https://darululoom.onrender.com
#   3. Rebuild + resync:
#        npm run build:android
#        npx cap sync android
#        cd android && ./gradlew assembleDebug   (or assembleRelease)
#
# Empty (default): same-origin — only correct for web builds. On Android this
# means sync is dormant until VITE_API_BASE is set.
VITE_API_BASE=
